+-----------------------------------------------------------------------
| Running ${PKGSTEM} on OpenBSD
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------

Getting started
===============
Run `renpy` to start the Ren'Py launcher, or `renpy /path/to/project`
to skip the launcher and run one project directly.

On first use the launcher asks for a projects directory; creating and
choosing it uses a dialog helper (x11/Xdialog, installed as a
dependency).

Live2D
======
Ren'Py's optional Live2D animation support requires Live2D Cubism
Core, a proprietary binary-only library with no OpenBSD version.
Games that use Live2D animations will not be able to display them,
and typically will not run at all.
